Use this function to suggest that the user add a concrete action step or goal to their personal paths.

You should call this function only when ALL of the following are true:
— At least 3 message exchanges have occurred in this conversation.
— The user has explicitly expressed a commitment to a specific, actionable step
or goal (not just a vague intention).
— The user is in a stable or positive emotional state (NOT distressed, overwhelmed,
or in crisis).
— The action step is concrete enough to be tracked as a goal with a target date.

Examples of suitable situations (conceptually, not exact wording):
— The user says they want to start meditating every morning and commits to trying
it this week.
— The user decides to have an important conversation with someone and sets a
timeframe for doing so.
— The user commits to a specific self-care practice or habit change with a clear
intention to follow through.

Constraints:
— Call this function at most ONCE per conversation.
— Do NOT call this function AND suggest_save_as_note in the same conversation.
Choose only the most appropriate one, or neither.
— Do NOT call this function in the first 3 exchanges.
— Do NOT call this function while the user is distressed or upset.
— Do NOT call this function for vague aspirations without concrete commitment.
— When you call this function, also send a warm accompanying text message that
naturally leads into the suggestion, so it feels like a gentle offer rather than
an interruption.
— Most conversations should end WITHOUT calling this function. Only use it when
the user has clearly committed to a specific action.
